 goal of nutrition support is to ensure that patients receive adequate nutrients to meet their needs when they cannot do so through regular eating. Overall, nutrition support plays a vital role in the recovery and management of patients with significant health challenges.", "TAPIA MJ:Tapia MJ is a researcher and author known for their contributions to the field of diabetes management, particularly in relation to parenteral nutrition. They have co-authored studies that examine the prevalence of diabetes and its management within the context of parenteral nutrition. Additionally, Tapia MJ played a significant role in a study focused on parenteral nutrition-associated hyperglycemia, which was published in the journal Diabetes Care. Their work highlights the critical intersection of diabetes care and nutritional support in clinical settings.", "OCÓN J:Ocón J is a contributor to research on insulin therapy and metabolic control in patients on total parenteral nutrition.", "CABREJAS-GÓMEZ C:Cabrejas-Gómez C is part of the study group focusing on hyperglycemia in parenteral nutrition.", "BALLENTEROS-POMAR MD:Ballenteros-Pomar MD is a researcher involved in the study of diabetes management in parenteral nutrition.", "GONZALEZ INFANTINO CA:Gonzalez Infantino CA is an author who studied hyperglycemia and hypoalbuminemia as mortality factors in patients with enteral feeding.", "GONZÁLEZ CD:González CD is a researcher who contributed to studies on hyperglycemia in patients receiving enteral nutrition.", "SANCHEZ R:Sanchez R is an author involved in research on hyperglycemia and its effects on patients with enteral feeding.", "PRESNER N:Presner N is a researcher who studied the impact of hyperglycemia in enteral feeding patients.", "LASSEN K:Lassen K is a notable contributor in the field of perioperative care, particularly in colorectal surgery and pancreaticoduodenectomy. They have played a significant role in the consensus review of optimal perioperative care practices for colorectal surgery. Additionally, Lassen K has contributed to the development of guidelines for perioperative care in pancreaticoduodenectomy, specifically as an author for the guidelines established by the ERAS Society. Their research and contributions are instrumental in enhancing the standards of care in these surgical areas.", "COOLSEN MM:Coolsen MM is involved in research comparing feeding regimes after pancreaticoduodenectomy.", "SLIM K:Slim K is a researcher who contributed to guidelines for the care of patients undergoing pancreaticoduodenectomy.", "DE AGUILAR- NACIMIENTO JE:De Aguilar-Nacimiento JE is a contributor to research on postoperative care in pancreaticoduodenectomy.", "SCHÄFER M:Schäfer M is a researcher and author who has made significant contributions to the field of medicine. They have played a key role in developing guidelines for managing patients after pancreaticoduodenectomy, a complex surgical procedure. Additionally, Schäfer M has conducted studies on immunonutrition, exploring its implications and benefits in patient care. Their work reflects a commitment to improving outcomes for patients through evidence-based practices and innovative nutritional strategies.", "GUILBAUD T:Guilbaud T is a researcher who compared different feeding regimes after pancreaticoduodenectomy."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}